/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Unlike conventional LEDs requiring high-temperature synthesis, perovskite LEDs can be fabricated at lower temperatures, reducing production costs. Their high efficiency, solution processability, tunable bandgap for versatile color emission, and easy deposition make them frontrunners for next-generation color displays, lighting solutions, and optical communication systems. Similar to solar cells, the primary hurdle for perovskite LEDs is limited operational stability. However, their low-cost and high-efficiency nature offers a compelling advantage.)
/E (Unlike conventional LEDs requiring high-temperature synthesis, perovskite LEDs can be fabricated at lower temperatures, reducing production costs. Their high efficiency, solution processability, tunable bandgap for versatile color emission, and easy deposition make them frontrunners for next-generation color displays, lighting solutions, and optical communication systems. Similar to solar cells, the primary hurdle for perovskite LEDs is limited operational stability. However, their low-cost and high-efficiency nature offers a compelling advantage.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
