/E (The decision to pursue graduate studies is a pivotal moment in the lives of many students, and one that almost all undergraduates are rattled by at one point of time or another. It marks a significant crossroads where questions, doubts, and uncertainties abound. With numerous factors to consider, such as career prospects, financial implications, and personal aspirations, it's no wonder that students often find themselves confused when contemplating the path of higher education. We asked Mandar Gadre, an alumnus of our department, who pursued higher studies in Materials Science and Engineering to shed more light onto this topic, and to provide his insights to help students better navigate this complex terrain. )
