347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (One unique thing that IITB offers over most other universities is allowing students to take courses from various departments ranging from 2xx to 8xx levels of difficulty. This enables one to pursue courses pertaining to their field of interest and develop stronger research fundamentals. It is true that mandatory coursework takes up a lot of your time and, in most cases, is exhausting enough to put you off from taking extra courses. But especially in the MEMS department, only the fundamentals are covered at the undergraduate level. Taking additional \(usually senior-level\) courses is beneficial to go towards a specific field.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
