>>
endobj
351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 644 0 R
/E (My interest in pursuing research in materials science started while doing MM152, thanks to Prof. Parag Bhargava. Before joining the MEMS department as an undergraduate,I was already interested in chemistry. In fact, that is partly the reason that motivated me to join here. During pre-registration for the third semester, many of my seniors mentioned that pursuing an electrical minor would be beneficial since it is closely related to material science. I took up EE207 \(Electronic Devices and Circuits\) because it seemed the closest. I quite enjoyed the course and got into the field of semiconductors. I took up MM474 \(Thin Film Science and Technology\) to gain insight into the semiconductor fabrication process.I was more into experimental work than theoretical, so I wanted to take up courses on characterisation because basic knowledge of these techniques is a must for working in any lab. The courses I took up for the same are MM206 \(Experimental Techniques in Material Science, 4th Sem\) and CH521 \(Interpretative Molecular Spectroscopy, 5th Sem\).)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
