367 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Department of Metallurgical Engineering and Materials Science at IIT Bombay recently hosted an Open Day, welcoming over 400 school students from 10 different schools, spanning from 8th grade and above. This event, held on August 26, 2023, as part of the IOE outreach program, provided a unique opportunity for young minds to explore the fascinating world of metallurgical engineering and materials science.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
368 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In the lecture hall area of IIT Bombay, the Open Day was lively with students showing off demonstration, exhibits, and experiments. Led by enthusiastic department students, these activities highlighted the field's dynamism, stirring curiosity and fostering a love for learning)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
369 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Among the standout demonstrations were explorations of concepts like scale and size, where students gained insights into the microscopic world and its implications on materials properties. Additionally, innovative experiments such as generating heat and electricity from motion, creating music from unconventional materials, and even designing their own superheroes through 3D printing captured the imaginations of participants.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
